the knight away:** Nxd3 wins a pawn, and the knight on d3 then also attacks the
c1 rook and the b2 pawn. - **If White plays Nd5:** Black has two knights
covering d5, so after the trades Black comes out ahead. - **If White just
defends with Rfd1 or Rcd1:** Black continues calmly with Rac8 and has a
