[%cachewrite 1806] Black is materially much worse. White's a5 passer is
dangerous, so I want to put pressure on it. Moving the bishop to d8 opens the
d8-c7-b6-a5 diagonal. The a5 pawn is then attacked by both the rook and the
bishop, and only White's rook on b5 defends it. If White replies Nc7 to hit the
rook, Bxc7 wins the knight. If White replies Rb8, Rxb8 answers it. } 32. b4 Kf8
